  "schema": "ancora.parity.scenario.v1",
  "id": "s04-entry-order",
  "title": "The E2E organization with codes that do not sort in entry order",
  "notes": [
    "Same data and order as s01, but group G1 has the code Z1 and group G2 the code A2, and the teachers TA and TB have the codes TZ and TB0.",
    "generar() reads the groups in id order. Legacy ids sort in entry order (replica ids, PAR-110), so the legacy result is the E2E one. The engine ids of the sync are numbered with the entity id (creation order), so Drupal gives the same result; ids made of the codes alone would put group A2 (G2) first and give another timetable."
  ],
